<title>USA: Hertz Corp sells $250 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Hertz Corp sells $250 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Hertz Corp was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Hertz Corp is the world's largest car rental company.</p>
<p>BORROWER HERTZ CORP</p>
<p>AMT $25O MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 7/1/2004</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD 7.00 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD +55 BPS    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
